# Line endings and diff behaviour.
#
# Every text blob currently in this repo is stored LF-only (verified, not assumed). This
# file exists to keep it that way: the two developers work on Windows and macOS, and a
# contributor whose `core.autocrlf` is unset would otherwise commit CRLF and produce a
# whole-file diff on a one-line change.
#
# Nothing here rewrites existing files. It only governs what happens on future check-in.

# Normalise all text to LF in the repository, whatever the working tree uses.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must be LF even in the working tree — CRLF breaks bash parsing outright.
*.sh text eol=lf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Binary — never diff, never line-ending-convert, never merge.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.parquet  binary
*.png      binary
*.jpg      binary
*.jpeg     binary
*.pdf      binary
*.docx     binary
*.xlsx     binary
*.pyd      binary
*.onnx     binary

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Notebooks.
#
# Committed WITH outputs on purpose (see notebooks/README.md), so they are large and
# their diffs are noisy. Marked as text so line endings stay normalised, but excluded
# from GitHub's diff view by default — a reviewer wants the rendered notebook, not 40k
# lines of base64 PNG.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.ipynb text eol=lf linguist-documentation

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GitHub language statistics.
#
# Without this the repo reads as ~99% "Jupyter Notebook" because the committed outputs
# dominate by byte count. The notebooks are genuinely the substance here, so they still
# count — but generated artifacts and shipped data should not.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
reports/**      linguist-documentation
data/**         linguist-vendored
*.md            linguist-documentation
